    "schemaxis.whispercpp.correct/3": {
      "guide": "docs/whispercpp.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Apply authored per-cue text replacements, whole-cue deletions and whole-interval timing edits by original source index, with a declared review status and note, to one retained whisper.cpp machine segments.json and publish a separately versioned reviewed timed-text document (reviewed/3), transcript text, SRT, WebVTT and an exact ledger that maps each published cue to its source cue and records the original and edited time of every retimed cue. Host-only: whisper-cli is never launched. correct/1, correct/2, reviewed/1 and reviewed/2 promise the original timestamps and are unchanged.",
        "assumptions": "A retained unedited machine segments.json (schemaxis.whispercpp.segments/1) with at least one cue, within the shared timed-text budgets, and its SHA-256 copied from the draft the author reviewed. Replacements, deletions and timing edits name source indices of that draft; the author states each new interval as integer elapsed milliseconds.",
        "constraints": "Host-only and not native-qualified: no audio, model or recognition run is read or repeated, there is no qualification record for this route, and a transcription receipt for the provider does not qualify it. At most 512 cues, 256 characters per cue and 32768 in total; at most 512 replacements, deletions and timing edits; note 1 to 500 plain-text characters. The finished cue set must be ordered, nonoverlapping and 0 <= start < end <= the audio duration rounded up to a millisecond; times are never clamped, reordered or rounded, and cues are never added, split or merged. Deleting every cue of a nonempty draft is allowed and publishes empty captions; an original draft with zero cues and a reviewed document used as a draft are refused; captionReview is refused when nothing is retained. The review status and every edited time are the author's declaration; reviewer identity, hearing the audio, audio synchronization, accuracy, readability and accessibility are not verified or certified.",
        "inspection": "Capture the draft bytes, require them to hash to basisSha256, then derive every publication again from those bytes and the authored edits and compare each file byte for byte: reviewed-segments.json (schemaxis.timedtext.reviewed/3, parsed by the shared validator, which proves that the declared edited indices are exactly the retained cues whose published interval differs from the recorded original and that the published times are ordered, nonoverlapping and inside the audio), transcript.txt, captions.srt, captions.vtt, the corrections.json ledger (replacements and timing edits, each with the original draft times as originalStartMs/originalEndMs and the published times as startMs/endMs; deletions with original text and originalStartMs/originalEndMs only; and the published-to-source mapping) and the optional caption-review.json recomputed on the retained text and published times. Membership is exact and any native launcher, submission or log is a failure.",
        "recovery": "CORRECTIONS_STALE: review the current draft and copy its sha256 into basisSha256. TIMING_DUPLICATE, TIMING_DELETION_CONFLICT, TIMING_INTERVAL_INVALID, DELETION_DUPLICATE, CORRECTION_DELETION_CONFLICT, CORRECTION_DUPLICATE, CORRECTION_NOOP, CORRECTION_TEXT_INVALID and CORRECTIONS_NOTE_INVALID name the entry to fix at its location. TIMING_NOOP: remove the entry equal to the existing interval. TIMING_OVERLAP and TIMING_AFTER_AUDIO name the offending edit: adjust it or its neighbour so the finished cues are ordered, nonoverlapping and inside the audio. TIMING_INDEX_INVALID, DELETION_INDEX_INVALID and CORRECTION_INDEX_INVALID: use a source index of the draft. CORRECTIONS_STATUS_CONFLICT: use human-corrected with at least one replacement, deletion or timing edit, or human-reviewed-unchanged with none. DRAFT_NOT_MACHINE_DRAFT: edit the original machine draft, not a reviewed document. CAPTION_REVIEW_EMPTY: omit captionReview or keep a cue. DRAFT_SOURCE_MISSING: the draft file or a directory on its path does not exist; INVALID_DRAFT_SOURCE: the path is relative, a link, a directory, not a regular file or over the byte budget. MISSING_ARGUMENT: add the absent required member. TIMED_TEXT_RESOURCE_LIMIT at $.corrections[n].text: shorten replacements or delete cues so the transcript stays within 32768 characters. UNKNOWN_ARGUMENT/INVALID_ARGUMENT: remove or fix the located member (times are integers, never floats or booleans). TIMED_TEXT_*: the draft breaks the shared contract or budgets. VERIFICATION_FAILED: a retained file differs from independent replay; rerun from the declared input."
      },
