    "schemaxis.whispercpp.captions/1": {
      "guide": "docs/whispercpp.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Break each cue of one pinned timed transcript (a machine segments.json or a reviewed/1, /2 or /3 document) into explicit lines of at most maxLineCodePoints Unicode code points and at most maxLines lines, and publish captions.srt, captions.vtt and caption-layout.json. Host-only: whisper-cli is never launched. A break replaces one isolated ordinary space (a run of two or more adjacent spaces is never broken or normalised), so every word, cue index and millisecond is unchanged and joining the lines of a cue with one space restores its text exactly; the source status is carried unchanged and is never promoted.",
        "assumptions": "A retained timed-text document read by the shared closed validator (at most 4MiB, 512 cues, 256 characters per cue, 32768 in total) and its SHA-256 copied from the document the author reviewed. Cue text may hold runs of adjacent ordinary spaces; they are kept inside an unbreakable run and never normalised. Both bounds are authored: maxLineCodePoints 8 to 80 and maxLines 1 to 3.",
        "constraints": "Host-only and not native-qualified: no audio, model or recognition run is read or repeated, there is no qualification record for this route, and a transcription receipt does not qualify it. Lengths are Unicode code points of the source text, not grapheme clusters, display width, font metrics or readability. The layout is the fewest lines, then the smallest sum of squared line lengths, then the earliest breaks. An unbreakable run longer than maxLineCodePoints or a cue that needs more than maxLines is refused naming the cue; nothing is split inside a run, truncated, retimed or widened, and a script written without spaces can be refused although it looks narrow. SRT payload is plain text and WebVTT escapes & < > once per line; no cue settings, styles or speaker labels. The review status and language are the source author's declarations; accuracy, readability, accessibility, synchronization and reviewer identity are not verified or certified. Consumers can be stricter: the FFmpeg review movie accepts plain SRT of at most four lines per cue and refuses < > { } and backslash and format characters.",
        "inspection": "Hold the source bytes, require them to hash to sourceSha256, derive every publication again from those bytes and the authored bounds and compare each file byte for byte: captions.srt, captions.vtt and the canonical caption-layout.json, then check the typed authored document, plan, receipt (runtime host-only, no executable or profile), exact membership (any native launcher, submission, log, link or planted .dispatch content is a failure), the source capture binding and the retained result. Nothing stored is trusted.",
        "recovery": "LAYOUT_SOURCE_STALE: review the current source and copy its sha256 into sourceSha256. LAYOUT_SOURCE_CHANGED: the source changed while the layout ran; rerun. INVALID_SOURCE: use an absolute local .json regular file of at most 4MiB (no link, device, directory or FIFO). SOURCE_MISSING: the file or a directory on its path does not exist. TIMED_TEXT_*: the source breaks the shared contract or budgets. LAYOUT_WORD_TOO_LONG: raise maxLineCodePoints or correct the unbreakable run (a word, or words joined by a no-break space or by two or more adjacent ordinary spaces). LAYOUT_TOO_MANY_LINES: raise maxLines or maxLineCodePoints. INVALID_ARGUMENT: bounds are integers 8 to 80 and 1 to 3. UNKNOWN_ARGUMENT/MISSING_ARGUMENT: use exactly the declared members. RUNNER_CANCELLED/RUNNER_TIMED_OUT: rerun into a fresh directory. VERIFICATION_FAILED: a retained file differs from independent replay; rerun from the declared input."
      },
